  "_title_nl": "Mail administration: protection with incoming checks, message size, rates, encryption and relay",
  "_note_nl": "What you see: The Protection page with four cards: Incoming mail (checks on the sending server), Message size (the one home of largest message, size of one upload, recipients, headers), Rates (connections at the same time, commands, sender, recipient, signed-in user) and Encryption and relay (encryption, relay server on two lines, server certificates), with the save row at the bottom.",
  "Mail administration: protection with incoming checks, message size, rates, encryption and relay": "",
  "Search protection settings": "",
  "What the server refuses, how large and how fast mail may be, and when it insists on encryption. Changes apply to every domain on this server as soon as you save.": "",
  "Incoming mail": "",
  "Checks on the sending server before a message is accepted. Together they stop most spam before anyone sees it.": "",
  "Delay first-time senders": "",
  "A server we have not seen before is asked to try again in a few minutes. Real mail servers do, most spam senders do not.": "",
  "Refuse mail from servers on a block list": "",
  "The sending address is looked up in these DNS block lists. A listed server is refused before the message is read.": "",
